                     <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_437">Winchester, Hampshire.
                           Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St Paul, and St
                           Swithun</orgName><p><q>Explicit liber magistri Petri Blesensis de
                              caritate sive de vera amicitia quem scripsit quidam monachus ecclesie
                              Sancti Swithuni Wintonie F<supplied>rat</supplied>er
                                 W<supplied>...</supplied>s d<supplied>e</supplied>
                              <supplied>...</supplied>a</q>. The Winchester inscription is on fol.
                           73v, all from <q>Quem</q> being partly erased. Since there is no change
                           of hand at this point it seems possible that the inscription is taken
                           over from the exemplar. The last word probably begins <q>Longe</q>,
                           followed by about 4 letters and <q>a</q>. [The index card marks this
                           provenance as uncertain, but this is not reflected in
                        MLGB2].</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_189">Durham. Benedictine
                           cathedral priory of St Cuthbert</orgName><p>Later at Durham. <q>Liber
                              sancti Cuthberti et Ricardi Bell, prioris Dunelm.</q></p><p><q>Iste
                              liber assignatus novo armariolo in claustro ecclesie Dunelm. per
                              venerabilem patrem magistrum <persName>Johannem Aukland</persName>,
                              priorem eiusdem ecclesie.</q></p><p>On fol. 8r:
                           <q>Emyldon</q>.</p><p>Letter mark "E" (fol. 8r).</p><q type="pressmark"
                           >E</q></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Archbishop
                           Laud</persName> 1633.</provenance>
